6.2 Questions that remain unresolved
The main uncertainties concern:

the precise migration corridors used during the Yamnaya expansion;
genetic substructure within the populations involved;
intermediate populations along the eastward route into Inner Asia;
uneven geographic sampling across Eurasia;
limited community-level mobility and kinship evidence outside Europe;
chronological resolution within individual migration episodes;
the independent linguistic evidence needed to evaluate proposed language homelands; and
the social mechanisms through which languages may have spread between migrating and local populations.

